Our contributions:
\begin{enumerate}
    \item \textbf{The correlation-selection gap.}
    $\rho{=}0.38$ on the primary test bed (up to 0.45 on a ceiling-effect control) coexists with selection that fails to outperform cost-free greedy decoding ($T{=}0$, F1${=}0.663$) despite 13--18~pp oracle headroom. Single-metric evaluation risks selecting the wrong signal.

    \item \textbf{Two failure mechanisms.}
    (a)~\textit{Instance degeneracy}: MBR utility correlates positively with F1 within instances (median $\rho{=}0.52$), but 21--58\% of instances produce identical F1 across all $N$ samples, eliminating headroom; on non-degenerate instances, MBR closes 23--41\% of the oracle gap.
    (b)~\textit{LP compression}: log-probability has median within-instance range of 0.041 nats ($\rho(\text{LP}, \text{F1}){=}0.248$); entity-token LP increases variance ($4{\times}$) but worsens selection, pointing to intrinsic overconfidence.

    \item \textbf{Diagnostic ablation chain.}
    A 4-seed free-form decoding ablation confirms NER compression is not caused by constrained decoding. Verbalized confidence is even more compressed, confirming compression is not LP-specific (Appendix~\ref{app:verbalized_confidence}). Rankings shift with task complexity and collapse at the capability boundary.
\end{enumerate}

tool_args.new_text:
Our contributions:
\begin{enumerate}
    \item \textbf{Two failure mechanisms.}
    We diagnose instance degeneracy and log-probability compression as mechanisms explaining why quality estimation signals fail to translate into selection gains in fine-tuned IE models.
    Instance degeneracy: MBR utility correlates positively with F1 within instances (median $\rho{=}0.52$), but 21--58\% of instances produce identical F1 across all $N$ samples, eliminating headroom; on non-degenerate instances, MBR closes 23--41\% of the oracle gap.
    LP compression: median within-instance range of 0.041 nats ($\rho(\text{LP}, \text{F1}){=}0.248$); entity-token LP increases variance ($4{\times}$) but worsens selection, pointing to intrinsic overconfidence.

    \item \textbf{Diagnostic ablation chain.}
    A five-layer ablation (free-form decoding, entity-token LP, verbalized confidence, non-tied subset, signal combinations) confirms these mechanisms are intrinsic to the fine-tuning regime. Signal rankings shift with task difficulty and collapse at the capability boundary.

    \item \textbf{Practical implication.}
    Greedy decoding ($T{=}0$, F1${=}0.663$) surpasses all $N{=}8$ selection strategies (best: 0.647) despite 13--18~pp oracle headroom---multi-sample selection adds cost without benefit under current signal families.
\end{enumerate}
